ca-certificates — installed as: ca-certificates-bundle
Licence declared by Alpine: MPL-2.0 AND MIT

Alpine's ca-certificates project, https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/ca-certificates
(built by the aport at https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable/main/ca-certificates).
The project has no licence file; its licences are stated in the headers of its files, and
those headers are reproduced here exactly.

What this image installs is ca-certificates-bundle: /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt, the
CA certificates generated from Mozilla's certdata.txt, which is under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0. That licence's text is alongside as MPL-2.0.txt, from SPDX's licence list.
Header of certdata.txt:

#
# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
# License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
# file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

The bundle is generated by mk-ca-bundle.pl, from curl, which the image does not contain.
Header of mk-ca-bundle.pl, for its copyright notice:

# * Copyright (C) Daniel Stenberg, <daniel@haxx.se>, et al.
# *
# * This software is licensed as described in the file COPYING, which
# * you should have received as part of this distribution. The terms
# * are also available at https://curl.se/docs/copyright.html.
# *
# * You may opt to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute and/or sell
# * copies of the Software, and permit persons to whom the Software is
# * furnished to do so, under the terms of the COPYING file.
# *
# * This software is distributed on an "AS IS" basis, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
# * KIND, either express or implied.
# *
# * SPDX-License-Identifier: curl

The project's MIT licence is c_rehash.c's, which belongs to the ca-certificates package
rather than ca-certificates-bundle, so it is not in this image either. Its header:

/* c_rehash.c - Create hash symlinks for certificates
